  "id": "automatic-process",
  "term": "automatic process",
  "definition": "An automatic process is a chain of actions produced by repeated or ongoing stimulation that goes on largely without attention. In this historical usage, it can refer either to inborn reflex-like activity or to well-practised actions that no longer need attention.",
